@startuml
!pragma useVerticalIf on
title "RootCanal: How to trace BLE Link-Layer PDUs (and HCI) with Wireshark\nWhat the built-in sniffers cover - and what they don't"
scale 0.9

' ------------------------------------------------------------------
' Participants
' ------------------------------------------------------------------
actor "User" as U
control "rootcanal process" as RC
control "Ctrl A\n(Central)" as CA
control "Ctrl B\n(Peripheral)" as CB
entity "PhyLayer\n(LOW_ENERGY / BR_EDR)" as PHY
entity "HciSniffer\n(LINKTYPE 201)" as HS
entity "BaseBandSniffer\n(LINKTYPE 255)" as BS
entity "Sniffer device\n(INFO log)" as SNIF
entity "LE Phy TCP server\n(link_ble_port 6404)" as LEPS
entity "Wireshark" as WS

note right of RC
  RootCanal does **not** emit BLE Link-Layer PDUs in a
  format Wireshark natively dissects out of the box.
  Below are the three built-in tracing options and exactly
  what each one captures.
end note

== Option A - HCI sniffer - HCI layer (Wireshark-native) ==

U -> RC: launch with --enable_hci_sniffer\n(default hci port 6402)
RC -> HS: wrap HciSocketTransport in HciSniffer per host,\nlinktype 201 = LINKTYPE_BLUETOOTH_HCI_H4_WITH_PHDR
HS -> WS: writes rootcanal_DEVICEID_ADDR.pcap\n(4-byte direction + H4 type byte + HCI payload)
note right
  Wireshark "Analyze -> Decode As" auto-dissects HCI H4.
  You see HCI_LE_* commands/events, ACL data and L2CAP.
  This is HCI, NOT the on-air LL PDUs.
end note

== Option B - Baseband sniffer - BR/EDR only ==

U -> RC: launch with --enable_baseband_sniffer
RC -> BS: register BaseBandSniffer on BR_EDR phy
BS -> WS: writes baseband.pcap, linktype 255 =\nLINKTYPE_BLUETOOTH_BREDR_BB
note right
  From baseband_sniffer.cc this only handles
  PacketType::PAGE and PacketType::LMP, synthesising
  FHS/DM1 BR-EDR baseband records.
  **BLE LL PDUs are NOT captured by this option.**
end note

== Option C - Sniffer device - LL packets to log, not pcap ==

U -> RC: test port: add sniffer ADDR\n   add_device_to_phy ID LE_PHY_ID
RC -> SNIF: register a Sniffer Device on the LE phy
PHY -> SNIF: every LL packet whose src/dst matches\n   (ADV, SCAN, CONNECT, LLCP, ACL, ...)
SNIF -> RC: INFO log: DIRECTION src -> dst (Type ...)
note right
  Great for seeing which LL PDUs flow on the virtual air
  and in which direction, but only to the console/logs -
  not dissected by Wireshark.
end note

== Option D - RAW LE LL PDUs via the LE Phy TCP port - custom framing ==

U -> LEPS: TCP connect to --link_ble_port (default 6404)
note right LEPS
  This port is served by LinkLayerSocketDevice.
  Each message frame = 4-byte little-endian length prefix
  + serialized LinkLayerPacket (from packets/link_layer_packets.pdl).
  A client connected here is itself a PhyDevice on the LE
  phy: it can OBSERVE every LL PDU the controllers exchange,
  and can even INJECT LL PDUs back.
end note
PHY -> LEPS: PhyLayer::Send -> LinkLayerSocketDevice::ReceiveLinkLayerPacket
LEPS -> U: length prefix (uint32 LE) + LL packet bytes
U -> U: parse with packets/link_layer_packets.pdl\n   (these are RootCanal's OWN LL PDU encodings:\n   LE_LEGACY_ADVERTISING_PDU=0x0B, LE_SCAN, LE_CONNECT,\n   LLCP=0x41, ACL, ISO...). Wireshark does NOT parse\n   this custom format directly.

== To get true BLE on-air LL PDUs dissected in Wireshark ==

note right
  You must write a converter of your own:
    1. capture via Option D (LE phy port)
       or Option C (sniffer device),
    2. translate each RootCanal LinkLayerPacket into the
       Bluetooth LE LL PDU byte layout,
    3. write PCAP records with linktype
       LINKTYPE_BLUETOOTH_LE_LL (223) or
       LINKTYPE_BLUETOOTH_LE_LL_WITH_PHDR (256).
  Then Wireshark dissects ADV_IND, SCAN_REQ, CONNECT_IND,
  LLCP control PDUs (LL_VERSION_IND, LL_FEATURE_REQ, ...)
  and BLE data PDUs natively.
end note

== Deciding which to use ==

note over RC, WS
  +----------------------------+---------------------+-------------------------+
  | what you want              | built-in option     | wireshark dissects ?    |
  +----------------------------+---------------------+-------------------------+
  | HCI commands / events      | --enable_hci_sniffer| YES (LINKTYPE 201 H4)   |
  | BR/EDR baseband (PAGE,LMP) | --enable_baseband_sn| YES (LINKTYPE 255 BREDR)|
  | Realtime LL flow (LE)      | sniffer device /    | console log / custom,   |
  |                            | LE phy port 6404    | not native              |
  | True BLE LE LL PDU pcap    | (none built-in)     | requires your converter |
  +----------------------------+---------------------+-------------------------+
end note

@enduml